# @hub-lanes

# ── LANE RE-PROBE (2026-09-23, BH-1687) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Every 5 min: re-probe the runner lanes (codex, openrouter, fireworks, grok)
# marked down in state/lane-down/, so a lane that comes back clears itself
# instead of waiting for the 6-hourly canary. The tick only probes records
# that are DUE (by default 30 min apart, 6h apart once an outage is a day old),
# at most 4 per tick under a 600s deadline, and a lane down 24h raises ONE
# standing warn per outage. The numbers are the lane's knobs. flock -n dedupe: a tick that overlaps the last one exits.
# docs/SCHEDULER.md §6.
*/5 * * * * /root/harness/bin/hub-lease.sh check && /root/harness/bin/lane-reprobe.sh >> /root/harness/logs/lane-reprobe.log 2>&1
